# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PetCare .gitignore
#
# The intent: the code is shared, the products and anything machine-specific
# are not.  Be generous here -- a repository that accumulates one PNG per test
# per candidate over 30k targets stops being cloneable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
.tox/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- outputs: keep the code in git, not the products ----------------------
out/
out_*/
outputs/
results/
run_*/
*.log

# per-candidate products, wherever they land
petcare.json
summary.csv
report*.html
**/report_c*.html
**/dedup_annotated.csv
**/known_annotated.csv

# --- caches and downloads -------------------------------------------------
# These belong outside any synced folder (see petcare/cache.py); ignored here
# as well in case someone points $PETCARE_CACHE at the checkout.
cache/
.cache/
mastDownload/
tesscut/
*.zip

# --- data: never in git ---------------------------------------------------
*.fits
*.fits.gz
*.fits.fz
*.npz
!examples/*/data/**/*.npz
*.parquet
*.pq
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.feather

# figures: every test writes them, none of them belong here
*.png
*.pdf
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
!docs/*.svg

# --- internal-only --------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-specific driver scripts and anything with a hardcoded path.  The
# local master driver lives outside this repository on purpose;
# these patterns catch a stray copy.
local/
local_*.py
*_local.py
env.sh
.env
secrets*

# calibration: the sample definitions are shared, the run products are not
calibration/out/
calibration/runs/
calibration/*.csv
!calibration/samples/*.csv

# --- internal design notes ------------------------------------------------
# DESIGN_NOTES.md is the working document for this project: hardcoded paths,
# per-star validation numbers, failure post-mortems, and notes addressed to
# the two people building it.  The shared documentation is README.md.
DESIGN_NOTES.md
